      "text": "the start        = the person types, for example: dmap map dmap.py - the tool keeps two things, the job name \"map\" and the code file dmap.py, and starts that job    (main, parse_within)\nthe blocks       = every block of the code with its first and last line - a named piece of a python file, a heading of a document, a tag or a named piece of a web page - they exist only so the answer can name a real block and point at real lines    (block_spans, md_spans, html_spans, tag_spans, script_regions, js_spans, brace_delta)\nthe map so far   = the explanations already written for this file, read from the file that sits beside the code, or an empty one when this is the first    (load_map, load_existing)\nthe ask          = the ask text for claude, built from all of that: the code with a number in front of every line, the blocks with their lines, the explanations already written, and the new text    (numbered, cmd_map)\nthe answer       = claude says which lines each name of the new text covers, and a gate reads that answer - the lines must sit inside the file and inside the block, every named block must be real, and the line the new text hangs on must be a real line of the parent - a broken rule goes back to claude with the rule named, up to eight times    (ask_claude, check_entry, check_spans, part_chunk, chunks_of, head_token, part_lines, expand)\nthe writing      = the new explanation added at the end, the code lines no explanation touches yet counted, the whole map written back to disk    (recompute, fmt, cmd_map)\nthe other jobs   = show lists the explanations and how much of the code they cover, lines prints the numbered code, retext replaces the words of one explanation while keeping its names, undo removes the last one    (cmd_show, cmd_lines, cmd_retext, cmd_undo, part_line)\nafter a change   = sync matches the old lines of the code to the new ones, moves every line number of the map onto the new lines, then asks claude to repair only the words the change made wrong    (cmd_sync, old_lines_of, line_map, shift_map, shift_spans, check_sync)",
